MODULE CableDyn_DeckDriver
  !! The standalone `cabledyn` driver: read a MoorDyn-style `.dat` deck
  !! (doc/driver_format.md), solve it, and write a tabular `.out`. The
  !! production "model a simple case" entry point over the certified CableDyn core.
  !!
  !! A LINE is one object spanning End A (NodeA, fairlead/top) and End B (NodeB,
  !! anchor/bottom), built from an
  !! ordered list of SECTIONS (each a line type + length + user mesh) -- the OrcaFlex
  !! line-object model, so a composite power cable (bare + equivalent distributed buoyancy)
  !! is one line meshed per section, not several lines.
  !!
  !! Core path: the static initial condition for EI=0
  !! lines -- N independent lines, each spanning a Fixed anchor and a Coupled (held)
  !! fairlead, multi-section meshed (CableDyn_Line) + catenary-seeded (CableDyn_Catenary)
  !! + solved by load continuation (CableDyn_Static) on the optional penalty seabed.
  !! If dtM/TMax are supplied, the same persistent line models march dynamically with
  !! held coupled points or a strict motionFile time series and write one `.out` row
  !! per step, with optional uniform-current Morison drag and regular Airy-wave
  !! drag / Froude-Krylov / buoyancy wetting fields. Eligible finite-EI dynamic
  !! lines use the production cubic-Hermite lifecycle, including standalone flat or
  !! structured contact; the retained Cosserat wrapper is limited to the uncommon
  !! standalone topology that prescribes both endpoints.
  !! Point3 bodies, Body<N>/Connect/Free dynamic points, Rigid6 structural dynamics,
  !! free/fixed rigid rods with Rod<N>A/B end attachments, translational current/Airy/JONSWAP
  !! body hydro, finite-EI translational current/wave loading, and finite-EI
  !! held/prescribed translational endpoint motion, and finite-EI cables clamped or elastically
  !! connected to Rigid6 bodies and rods (moment returned) are supported within the documented
  !! scope. Features outside it parse but FAIL CLOSED with a clear error naming the unsupported
  !! feature.
